\ yaml>frame ( str -- val ), yaml-documents ( str -- arr ), frame>yaml ( val -- str ):
\ YAML read with the vendored libyaml into the values JSON gives, scalars typed
\ by YAML 1.2's core schema (so yes stays a string), aliases answering their
\ anchor's own object; written back as block-style YAML that reads as the same
\ value.

\ === yaml>frame: mappings, sequences, and the core schema's scalars ===
"name: Ann
age: 34
height: 1.75
tags: [a, b]
none: ~
empty:
flag: true
off: FALSE
answer: yes" yaml>frame to person
person@name . person@age . person@height . cr     \ Ann 34 1.75
person@tags . cr                                    \ [ "a" "b" ]
person@none . person@empty . cr                     \ null null
person@flag . person@off . cr                       \ :1 :0
person@answer dup . type-of . cr                    \ yes :string   YAML 1.1 would read true

clear

\ === numbers: decimal, signed, octal, hex, float, infinity, NaN, exact ===
"- -12
- +7
- 0o17
- 0x1F
- 1e3
- .5
- 1.
- -.inf
- .nan
- 123456789012345678901" yaml>frame to numbers
numbers . cr                                        \ [ -12 7 15 31 1000 0.5 1 -inf null 123456789012345678901 ]
numbers last type-of . cr                           \ :exact

clear

\ === strings: quoted, block, and plain text that is no number ===
"a: '12'
b: ""true""
c: 1_000
d: 12abc
e: |
  line one
  line two
f: >
  folded
  text" yaml>frame to texts
texts@a type-of . texts@b type-of . texts@c . texts@d . cr      \ :string :string 1_000 12abc
texts@e . cr                                                       \ line one / line two
texts@f . cr                                                       \ folded text

clear

\ === tags force a type ===
"a: !!str 12
b: !!float 3
c: !!int 0x10
d: !!null ~" yaml>frame to tagged
tagged@a type-of . tagged@b . tagged@c . tagged@d . cr          \ :string 3 16 null

clear

\ === aliases answer their anchor's object ===
"a: &pair [1, 2]
b: *pair" yaml>frame to shared
shared@a 99 add-last! drop shared@b . cr          \ [ 1 2 99 ]   one array under both keys
"&self {me: *self}" yaml>frame @me @me @me keys . cr   \ [ :me ]   a mapping holding itself
"&k key: 1
other: *k" yaml>frame @other . cr                 \ key   an anchored mapping key

clear

\ === documents ===
"" yaml>frame . cr                                 \ null   an empty stream
"a: 1
---
b: 2
---
- 3" yaml-documents . cr                           \ [ { :a 1 } { :b 2 } [ 3 ] ]
"" yaml-documents . cr                             \ [ ]
"--- &x [1]
--- [2]" yaml-documents size . cr                  \ 2   anchors are per document

clear

\ === frame>yaml: block style, quoting what would read back as another type ===
{ :count 1 :word "true" :list [ 1 2 ] } frame>yaml stdout write
\ word: 'true'
\ count: 1
\ list:
\ - 1
\ - 2
[ "yes" "12" "" "plain" "null" ] frame>yaml stdout write
\ - 'yes'
\ - '12'
\ - ''
\ - plain
\ - 'null'
{ :empty-list [ ] :empty-frame { } :text "two
lines" } frame>yaml stdout write
\ text: |-
\   two
\   lines
\ empty-list: []
\ empty-frame: {}
42 frame>yaml stdout write                          \ 42
:1 frame>yaml stdout write                          \ true
-1e999 frame>yaml stdout write                      \ -.inf

clear

\ === round trip: frame>yaml then yaml>frame answers an equal value ===
{ :n 1.5 :s "true" :l [ 1 "2" null :0 ] :f { :g "two
lines
" :h "café" } :big 123456789012345678901 } dup frame>yaml yaml>frame = . cr   \ 1
"{""a"": [1, ""x"", {""b"": null}], ""c"": true}" json>frame dup frame>yaml yaml>frame = . cr   \ 1

clear

\ === errors ===
"a: 1
---
b: 2" yaml>frame                                    \ (several documents)
"a: [1, 2" yaml>frame                               \ (unclosed flow sequence)
"a: *missing" yaml>frame                            \ (unknown alias)
"a: !!int hello" yaml>frame                         \ (value the tag does not take)
"a: !custom x" yaml>frame                           \ (unsupported tag)
"[1, 2]: x" yaml>frame                              \ (sequence as a mapping key)
"a: &n 5
*n : x" yaml>frame                                  \ (alias to a number as a mapping key)
{ :a :foo } frame>yaml                              \ (non-boolean symbol)
[ 1 2 ] vector frame>yaml                           \ (matrix)
1/3 frame>yaml                                      \ (non-integer exact)
42 yaml>frame                                       \ (not a string)
